{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception","id":763054,"title":"Tracking and Perception","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-11T06:28:29-08:00","id":763054,"title":"Tracking and Perception","content":"How exactly Perception can affect the tracking? Because it should - it's strange if werewolf in Hishu and Urhan have the same tracking ability, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T07:22:12-08:00","id":763084,"title":"","content":"They don't, Urhan provides a +1 to tracking rolls. They kinda missed the chance to add Wits to the lupine forms instead of flat bonuses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T07:26:02-08:00","id":763088,"title":"","content":"I think officially they're completely separate, though I have always ruled that the perception bonus from forms applies to any roll where heightened senses would be directly relevant. (could be investigation, survival, etc.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T07:52:11-08:00","id":763105,"title":"","content":"That's why improved Wits would have been better: No confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T09:11:28-08:00","id":763164,"title":"","content":"It's really bad and disappointing. I really hoped, that Uratha become great stalkers and trackers in 2.0 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T09:16:25-08:00","id":763170,"title":"","content":"It's a good thing they are great stalkers and trackers in second edition, then. Have you read the tracking section?<br /> <br /> If you really want additional Wits in another form you can manage it with the Favored Form merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T09:32:20-08:00","id":763177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception?p=763170#post763170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a good thing they are great stalkers and trackers in second edition, then. Have you read the tracking section?<br /> <br /> If you really want additional Wits in another form you can manage it with the Favored Form merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest the plan was: Urhan bonus to roll (+4) + IMPOSSIBLE SPOOR (the Uratha adds two successes to every successful roll) + HONED SENSES (The Uratha achieves an exceptional success on Perception rolls with 3 successes instead of 5) + may be SCENT THE UNNATURAL.<br /> That's what I mean great stalker/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2297-thebadwolf","name":"TheBadWolf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T10:22:16-08:00","id":763217,"title":"","content":"Each of those facets on their own make them great stalkers. Combined with tracking by blood, various perception and tracking bonuses and various other facets<br /> <br /> You could argue that tracking by scent (Survival), logically speaking, should grant a bonus in wolf forms equal to their perception bonus. But you could argue that the bonus is in being able to track by scent at all - as that's sort of representative of the heightened senses of the Uratha. The only real rub is that there is an issue of degrees and it's odd to be able to track equally by scent in Hishu as in Urhan. Nothing about the mechanics or fluff suggest that should be the case. But here we are. <br /> <br /> I say it's an oversight, so just houserule if you care, guys. Though I will say that Impossible Spoor and Honed Senses definitely should not interact. That would be ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T11:51:23-08:00","id":763300,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what the question is. A form's Perception bonus is already specifically added to the dice pool for Contested Tracking rolls (p95).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T11:56:49-08:00","id":763307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception?p=763164#post763164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really bad and disappointing. I really hoped, that Uratha become great stalkers and trackers in 2.0 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hm? They are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T12:30:08-08:00","id":763349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception?p=763300#post763300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what the question is. A form's Perception bonus is already specifically added to the dice pool for Contested Tracking rolls (p95).</div> </div> </div> </div> Yup. I missed it a few times when using the new tracking rules at my table, but it is in there in the text. So yes, Urhan are really, really good at tracking.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T02:08:00-08:00","id":763873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception?p=763349#post763349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup. I missed it a few times when using the new tracking rules at my table, but it is in there in the text. So yes, Urhan are really, really good at tracking.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But only in Contested Rolls, which I feel is kind of odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T05:59:11-08:00","id":763987,"title":"","content":"IIRC the rationale is that for the uncontested tracking you're shifting forms as needed and it would be too complicated to figure out the dice bonus, whereas for contested it's far more granular and you can add the bonus on a roll-by-roll basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T06:55:29-08:00","id":764018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception?p=763300#post763300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what the question is. A form's Perception bonus is already specifically added to the dice pool for Contested Tracking rolls (p95).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'll be..<br /> <br /> Forget everything I've said in this thread, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T21:41:36-08:00","id":764715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheBadWolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception?p=763177#post763177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest the plan was: Urhan bonus to roll (+4) + IMPOSSIBLE SPOOR (the Uratha adds two successes to every successful roll) + HONED SENSES (The Uratha achieves an exceptional success on Perception rolls with 3 successes instead of 5) + may be SCENT THE UNNATURAL.<br /> That's what I mean great stalker/</div> </div> </div> </div>A character could easily take all of these facets and be an absolutely unparalleled tracker. Honed Senses may not apply to Tracking rolls by RAI, but it's still useful for mundane Perception rolls, which can be useful for such a character to have when the Tracking rolls aren't the most appropriate resolution mechanic for the situation. Besides that, it's a very simple matter to house rule, which is what I do when I ST Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T04:54:42-08:00","id":764853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception?p=763987#post763987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC the rationale is that for the uncontested tracking you're shifting forms as needed and it would be too complicated to figure out the dice bonus, whereas for contested it's far more granular and you can add the bonus on a roll-by-roll basis.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see the distinction as being that clear. The different between Contested and non- is very minimal. I'd say you could easily take either mechanic and use it for both situations.<br /> <br /> e.g. Both people roll, but if it's &quot;contested&quot; then the tracked also adds Resolve to his rolls.<br /> or only the tracker rolls, but also loses (Tracked's Resolve) dice from the pool, if contested.<br /> <br /> Neither solution is perfect, but since uncontested can take even longer than contested, I don't see how Perception bonuses wouldn't apply. Contested doesn't even list a time for the extended checks, so it's a VERY loosely defined system.<br /> <br /> I suppose the real difference should be if you're hurrying or not, as opposed to being contested. If I'm in a huge rush, I probably don't want to find a place to hide and shift every time I want to double check the trail strength. However, if I know my prey is just sitting at home (uncontested!) why don't I consistently use my best tracking powers (Urhan)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","user":"FlailBot","date":".  more typos 11-13-2015, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T04:56:56-08:00","id":764855,"title":"","content":"If you know your prey is just sitting at home why would you be tracking them at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:21:55-08:00","id":764868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, if I know my prey is just sitting at home (uncontested!) why don't I consistently use my best tracking powers (Urhan)? </div> </div> </div>Because you're in the middle of a city, having to move between densely populated areas of humanity as well as deserted alleys. Humans tend to get nervous around wolves in their cities (or feral looking dogs) and soon the police and animal control are called. The situation rapidly escalates and you're soon faced with the choice of either running from the humans to avoid their attention, or fighting through them to save time. Either way, people have been Tweeting about the ruckus and it's now on the news, so your prey has fled his home, called on his support network, and you've now got a Contested Tracking situation. You'll probably still win, but it'll take longer. Meanwhile, your pack's giving you shit for being an idiot, and it's going to be a long time before they trust you with anything important again. Welcome to dog status for a while. There's Wolf-Blooded who get more important jobs than you.<br /> <br /> Or you could adapt to the situation, stay stealthy, use appropriate forms as needed, maintain the prey's ignorance, and be the unsurpassed *hunter* you're meant to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:30:23-08:00","id":764873,"title":"","content":"Although, if you had one of those fetishes that makes you look like a dog in wolf form (or use skin thief on one) then you might be able to get away with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T06:27:23-08:00","id":764891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception?p=764855#post764855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you know your prey is just sitting at home why would you be tracking them at all?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know where he lives. :-(<br /> <br /> @Bunyip: That seems like a particularly dramatic interpretation of a tracking roll. I can see sacrificing your various forms in a rushed roll. The need for expediency means taking more risks. But that's not the distinction I gather from unconstested vs. contested.<br /> <br /> Also, what if my non-contested roll is tracking someone who is camping? Surely urhan works then.<br /> <br /> *shrug* Clearly you have a very solid internal perception (lol) of the situation the rules are supposed to cover, which is great! Since you wrote them. :-p<br /> I will probably end up arguing with my GM about it though. :-)<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll scribble up some rushed/languid tracking rules and see if anyone thinks their work the virtual ink they're written on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T06:32:01-08:00","id":764893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf the Forsaken Second Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tracking takes time, and other events don\u2019t stop just because the hunter tracks her prey. The Storyteller should add encounters, distractions, and narrative obstacles to challenge the character and make tracking an exciting and integral part of the chronicle, rather than just a series of dice rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T08:03:48-08:00","id":764941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception?p=764893#post764893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Originally posted by <b>Werewolf the Forsaken Second Edition</b></i><br /> <i>Tracking takes time, and other events don\u2019t stop just because the hunter tracks her prey. The Storyteller should add encounters, distractions, and narrative obstacles to challenge the character and make tracking an exciting and integral part of the chronicle, rather than just a series of dice rolls.</i><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Which are then already covered by the lack of Perception bonus in the uncontested roll?<br /> <br /> Now, with that I shall excuse myself from the rest of this discussion. I think I understand everyone's perspectives, but I don't think we're working towards agreement here. More like<br /> &quot;This is my reasoning.&quot;<br /> &quot;Okay, I disagree. I'll do this instead.&quot;<br /> &quot;I accept your wacky nonsense.&quot;<br /> <br /> &lt;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T15:14:50-08:00","id":765180,"title":"","content":"(Assuming you're still reading this thread) There was a fair amount of facetiousness in the urban example - sorry about that, I blame posting after midnight.<br /> <br /> Anyway, let's see if I can explain the design decisions with a wilderness example like you suggested.<br /> <br /> First consideration - Werewolves are meant to be superlative hunters. The best of the best.<br /> <br /> Second consideration - Werewolves have five different forms, each of which is as natural for them to use as breathing. (Caveat: Without the Father's Form facet, Gauru is difficult to use for anything except fighting.)<br /> <br /> With those in mind, consider the prey camping somewhere in the woods. You know he's there, but not where. He doesn't know you're coming. Hence, it's Uncontested Tracking.<br /> <br /> If you were a wolf, you'd track him as a wolf. Nose down, find the scent trail, listen for clues. If you come across an obstacle, you deal with it like a wolf would. Stream (or other waterway)? Cross it and try and find the scent trail. If the prey has been clever, and moved up or down the stream, or backtracked, or anything else, you might never find the trail on the other side. If you were a wolf, you might give up. What if the stream is bigger? What if it's a river that's difficult to cross?<br /> <br /> If you were a human, you'd track the prey as a human. Try and find tracks, signs of where he has passed. Keep your eyes open, look for signs of smoke that might mean a campfire, see where other animals have been disturbed, try and listen out for clues. You've got no scent trail to follow, so if the prey crosses a rocky, stony patch, you might not find any tracks. What then? Cross to the other side and search for clues. If you don't find any, what comes next?<br /> <br /> You're a werewolf. You're better than both wolf and human. You know the prey is in the woods. You shift to Urhan and track by scent. The trail leads you to a river. You shift to Hishu or Dalu and climb into the trees to get a better view of the terrain. You search for smoke, you listen with keen ears for any sounds, your primal instincts tell you where other animals are present, and where they've cleared out to avoid the human.<br /> <br /> You find clues that suggest the prey had some kind of inflatable raft to cross the river. It's quite fast and would be a challenge to cross in Hishu or Urhan. You shift to Urshal and power your way across.On the other side you pick up the muddy footprints tat lead to the rocky hills that the prey has climbed. The ground is too loose for paws to comfortably traverse - it's more suited to hands - o you have options. Dalu works well because you can pick up some of the scent trail while climbing. If you have Father's Form, Gauru works wonderfully as your big hands and talons find all the good holds, your extra strength makes the climb simple, and your muzzle makes finding the scent trail simple.<br /> <br /> All through this, you've used your forms effectively and have covered the ground faster than any human or wolf could have. Your prey is blissfully unaware of the terror that's about to fall upon him.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And all this was accomplished via a single dice roll, which tells the ST if you're going to find the prey, lets her work out how long it should take (according to the narrative needs), and then devote more attention to working with the player to make the journey interesting (rivers, rocky cliffs etc.)<br /> <br /> Hopefully that helps explain what was in mind. Now, if your ST decides to give you a camping situation where the prey went straight from the car park to the camping site without any obstacles, feel free to argue that you do the entire tracking test in Urhan and that you should have the Perception bonus. Honestly, in that situation you shouldn't need the bonus because there's no challenge to finding the prey - if I was the ST in that instance, I wouldn't even call for a roll, because there is no significant challenge.<br /> <br /> EDIT EDIT: And both Uncontested/Contested deliberately don't define specific time periods. It depends on the narrative, the environment, and the players. Uncontested tracking attempts can be long, drawn out affairs where the werewolf takes her time and enjoys the experience. Similarly, Contested tracking can be furious, frantic affairs where the werewolf desperately needs to catch his evasive prey before it disappears for good. <br /> <br /> Just as easily, Uncontested can be the quick and dirty 'caught scent, tracked prey' experience, while Contested can be the slow and tense cat and mouse game between hunter and prey who is doing everything to confuse the trail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 11-13-2015, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T18:44:27-08:00","id":765280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/763054-tracking-and-perception?p=763873#post763873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But only in Contested Rolls, which I feel is kind of odd.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If someone doesn't want to be found it is contested. This could mean, they're specifically hiding from you and your pack - or just laying low in general.<br /> <br /> <br /> Being an ST, I'm finding the tracking almost ridiculous. It's really hard to hide from a werewolf on the hunt after you. At first I disliked how easy some of these things are for a werewolf, but I've embraced it now. It leads to a much different sort of game. Currently the game is going &quot;it's sooooo easy to take control, beat up people, hunt people down - but it all draws attention. At what point does being too obvious with your supernatural abilities get you in trouble - lunacy be damned?&quot; It's a tightrope for the wolf. How long can they hang around with the sheep before their nature betrays them?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5220,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","user":"Mother's Love","date":". 11-13-2015, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}